# pcsedit.ps2 - a construction session at the editor, with the mouse (`pcs 23`).
#
# ⭐ EVERY GESTURE IS ONE PRESS AND ONE RELEASE, and pcsui.inc's EdLoop makes the
# edit on the release (pcs.md §8).  checkpcs.py `ui` reads THIS FILE, works out
# where each press and release was, models the editor's answer from those
# points alone, and compares it with the fifteen bytes the machine recorded for
# the same gesture - and then the object area and the span database it left.
#
# ⚠ Card pixels, Y down.  The table is x 0..319 (world x = card x / 2), the kit
# is x 320..639, the tool column's icons are at card x 536..591, and the
# picker's cells are 8 x 8 from (432, 360).
# ⚠ `origin 0 0` because that is where the pointer IS when pcs starts: the mouse
# is relative, and a script that believed 320 240 put every press 320 left and
# 240 up of where it meant.
# ⚠ The gestures are FOUR SECONDS APART because a repaint is about a second and
# EdLoop does not sample the mouse during one: a press and release that both
# fall inside it are gone (pcsin.inc's header).  The hammer's gesture is two
# edits and two repaints, so it gets six.
origin 0 0
gap 300

# 1  the picker: row 1, column 5 - colour 32 + 17
at 1.000    move to 476 372
+0.300      click left

# 2  ⭐ the hand (the tool EdLoop starts with) drags BMP1, object 10, by (+10, +4)
at 5.000    move to 88 144
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 108 152
+0.400      up left

# 3  ⭐ a BMP4 out of the bin (template 8, pressed at world (212, 55)) and onto
#    the table, keeping the grab offset: its corner lands at (50, 140)
at 9.000    move to 424 110
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 110 284
+0.400      up left

# 4  a TARG1 out of the bin and let go OVER THE KIT - DELETEOBJ's case, and nothing
#    is added
at 13.000   move to 388 322
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 500 300
+0.400      up left

# 5  ⭐ TARG6, object 19, dragged off the table: deleted, and everything above it
#    renumbers
at 17.000   move to 202 194
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 400 200
+0.400      up left

# 6  a click on BMP2 that goes nowhere: no edit
at 21.000   move to 168 126
+0.300      click left

# 7  the POINTER
at 25.000   move to 560 40
+0.300      click left

# 8  ⭐ the divider's top-right corner (134, 30), pressed a unit below it, to (138, 40)
at 29.000   move to 268 62
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 276 80
+0.400      up left

# 9  ⛔ REFUSED: the right slingshot's apex (120, 184) dragged level with its base -
#    every Y equal, so ALIGNPOLY fails and the vertex goes back
at 33.000   move to 240 368
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 200 420
+0.400      up left

# 10  the HAMMER
at 37.000   move to 560 90
+0.300      click left

# 11  ⭐ the left lane guide's right edge: its midpoint (32, 152) is pasted, and then
#     dragged to (40, 150) - two edits, two records
at 41.000   move to 66 304
+0.300      down left
+0.300      move to 80 300
+0.400      up left

# 12  the SCISSORS
at 47.000   move to 560 60
+0.300      click left

# 13  ... and that new vertex cut away again
at 51.000   move to 80 300
+0.300      click left

# 14  ⭐ the left slingshot's corner (44, 210): a triangle cut is a DELETE
at 55.000   move to 88 418
+0.300      click left

# 15  the BRUSH
at 59.000   move to 560 116
+0.300      click left

# 16  ⭐ the centre post, painted colour 49
at 63.000   move to 156 364
+0.300      click left

# 17  ⭐ ... and painted 49 AGAIN, which clears it to 0 - unfilled and solid
at 67.000   move to 156 364
+0.300      click left

# 18  ⭐ bare table: SELECTPOLY misses and the brush paints the BACKDROP
at 71.000   move to 220 120
+0.300      click left

# 19  a library part cannot be painted: PAINTOBJ answers "took" and touches nothing
at 75.000   move to 168 126
+0.300      click left

# 20  ⭐ PLAY: the kit goes, the score strip comes, and a game runs on the table as
#     it stands - with no button pressed, so the ball waits in the lane and no
#     press here can be read as a gesture.  `q` ends the GAME, not the editor,
#     and the brush is still the tool when the kit comes back.  ⭐ The table
#     has to come back exactly as it was: the checker's final picture and
#     object area are taken after this.
at 79.000   move to 560 220
+0.300      click left
at 85.000   type "q"

# 21  the hammer, pressed where no edge is: SELECTPOINT misses
at 90.000   move to 560 90
+0.300      click left
at 94.000   move to 220 120
+0.300      click left

at 98.000   type "q"
